Subject: [PATCH] 58019: an old account's login needs a subscribed member's
 invitation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The founder's check (tester box 58019, 14 Oct): can anyone get Netai
without an invitation from an existing member? One real gap on the
server: an old Ally account logging in with an invitation. Its phone is
registered, so the gate answers „existing" and carries the lenient
attribution inviter, which asks no subscription. Any non-deleted
account's code or number let it in. Registration demands a subscribed
member; the login now does too (subscribedInviter: a subscribed code
owner, or else a subscriber's number).

Tests: the real gate under the live switches (invite_only,
netai_invite_only_login, invite_personal_code_only all on), which no test
ran before. It refuses no invitation, an unknown code, a lapsed member's
code, a company cohort code and social proof, and admits a subscriber's
own code. The typed subscriber's number still opens the door; it is
pinned as today's behaviour and put to Misho.

